From 084de4a7c276c3bf96555481eb9884d61c3c5e86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:15:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover vm_cow_defeatured_telemetry.c

Recover the three functions in vm_cow_defeatured_telemetry.c from the
KDK 27.0.1 DWARF and the RELEASE/DEVELOPMENT vmapple kernels:

  - vm_cow_defeatured_get_or_insert_entry() walks guard_count_head and
    compares process names with strncmp; a miss allocates a zeroed
    vm_cow_defeatured_guard_count_s (48 bytes) with kalloc_type and
    pushes it on the list.  The structure holds next, the proc_name_t
    name and the per-guard-code uint8_t counters.

  - vm_cow_defeatured_get_responsible_map_info() takes the current
    task's map and copies task_best_name() into the caller's buffer,
    returning false when there is no current task.

  - vm_cow_defeated_soft_mode_report() validates the guard code against
    VM_COW_DEFEATURED_GUARD_COUNT, accounts the violation under
    vm_cow_defeated_telemetry_lock and raises vm_map_guard_exception()
    outside the lock while the per-process report budget lasts.

The report is limited by the vm_cow_defeatured_soft_report_limit
tunable (default 10).  The reference line table pins the tunable at
line 69, the lock group and mutex at lines 74 and 76, the list head at
line 80 and the three function signatures at lines 88, 120 and 145.
The report's prototype is added in vm_cow_defeatured_telemetry.h at
reference line 44, the line vm_map.c sees it at.

The guard check at line 157 is a release_assert(): the RELEASE kernel
keeps the trap and its descriptor ("event_idx <
VM_COW_DEFEATURED_GUARD_COUNT") even though MACH_ASSERT is not defined
for the translation unit, which only release_assert() provides.

Add the three kGUARD_EXC_COW_DEFEATURED_* guard codes to
vm_statistics.h (13-15), move kGUARD_EXC_LARGE_ALLOCATION_TELEMETRY to
16 as the reference does, and derive VM_COW_DEFEATURED_GUARD_COUNT from
the FIRST/LAST enumerators.

The reference build performs the report-limit comparison in the
uint8_t domain (it compares the counter against the low byte of
limit - 1); the reconstruction keeps the recoverable source form.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
---
